0..79 Comment "/// A transport whose motive starts at another point than its moved path prints"
80..107 Comment "/// as the transport it is."
108..111 Comment "///"
112..190 Comment "/// A transport along `r` of `here(f)`, under a motive `Path(C, l, c)`, is the"
191..269 Comment "/// composite `here(f) then r` exactly when `l` is `f`. Reading that composite"
270..343 Comment "/// back takes the motive\'s start from `here(f)`. A motive that starts at"
344..417 Comment "/// `f then here(z)` is another type, which the composite does not spell."
418..421 Comment "///"
422..499 Comment "/// The printer writes a transport as a composite only where the moved path\'s"
500..569 Comment "/// start is the motive\'s. Otherwise it writes the transport in full."
570..573 Comment "///"
574..645 Comment "/// - see: #4218 — the printer wrote both transports as one composite"
646..712 Comment "/// - see: #754 — a returned composite of paths is written infix"
714..789 Comment "/// Motives whose fixed starts differ by the right unit of a variable path."
